# The dashboard's entire configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# Both of these are `NEXT_PUBLIC_`, which means **inlined into the browser
# bundle and readable by anyone with the URL**. That is correct for a hostname,
# and correct for the anon key, whose security model is Row-Level Security —
# it grants nothing on its own. It is correct for nothing else.
#
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only. Never set these on Vercel.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The service-role key bypasses RLS completely. It is used by exactly one thing
# — `npm run create-admin`, run once from your own machine to create the single
# operator account. If it ever reaches the deployed environment, every policy in
# migrations 0062-0064 stops meaning anything.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Used by `npm run check:limits`, which reads the CHECK constraints back out of
# the database to prove src/lib/limits.ts still describes it.
# Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string (pooler).
#
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgres://...
